{
  "slug": "js_object_properties",
  "course": "js",
  "order": 47,
  "url": "/js/js_object_properties.asp",
  "title": "JavaScript Object Properties",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "JavaScript Object Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Properties are key:value Pairs"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A JavaScript object is a collection of properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Properties can be changed, added, and deleted."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Accessing JavaScript Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can access object properties in these ways:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["Dot notation", "Bracket notation", "Expression"]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "// objectName.property\n\nlet age = person.age;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "//objectName[\"property\"]\n\nlet age = person[\"age\"];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "//objectName[expression]\n\nlet age = person[x];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "objectName.propertyName",
      "caption": "Dot Notation"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "person.firstname + \" is \" + person.age;",
      "caption": "Dot Notation"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties1"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "objectName[\"propertyName\"]",
      "caption": "Bracket Notation"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "person[\"firstname\"] + \" is \" + person[\"age\"];",
      "caption": "Bracket Notation"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties2"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In general, dot notation is preferred for readability and simplicity."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Bracket notation is necessary in some cases:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "The property name is stored in a variable:\nperson[myVariable]",
        "The property name is not a valid identifier:\nperson[\"last-name\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Bracket notation is useful when the property name is stored in a variable:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let n1 = \"firstName\";\n\nlet n2 = \"lastName\";\n\nlet name = person[n1] + \" \" + person[n2];",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties7"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Changing Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can change the value of a property:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "person.age = 10;",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties8"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Adding New Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can add a new property by simply giving it a value:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "person.nationality = \"English\";",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties3"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Deleting Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The delete keyword deletes a property from an object:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const person = {\n\n  firstName: \"John\",\n\n  lastName: \"Doe\",\n\n  age: 50,\n\n};\n\ndelete person.age;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const person = {\n\n  firstName: \"John\",\n\n  lastName: \"Doe\",\n\n  age: 50,\n\n};\n\ndelete person[\"age\"];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties4"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The delete keyword deletes both the value and the property."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "After deleting, the property is removed. Accessing it will return undefined."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Check if a Property Exists"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Use the in operator to check if a property exists in an object:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const person = {\n\n  firstName: \"John\",\n\n  lastName: \"Doe\"\n\n};\n\nlet result = (\"firstName\" in person);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_properties9"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Nested Objects"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Property values in an object can be other objects:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "myObj = {\n\n  name:\"John\",\n  age:30,\n\n  myCars: {\n    car1:\"Ford\",\n\n  car2:\"BMW\",\n    car3:\"Fiat\"\n\n    }\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "You can access nested objects using the dot notation or the bracket notation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "myObj.myCars.car2;",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "myObj.myCars[\"car2\"];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "myObj[\"myCars\"][\"car2\"];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let p1 = \"myCars\";\n\nlet p2 = \"car2\";\n\nmyObj[p1][p2];",
      "caption": "Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_object_nested"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Object properties are key:value pairs",
        "Access properties with dot notation or bracket notation",
        "Add, change, and delete properties using assignment and delete",
        "Use the in operator to check if a property exists"
      ]
    },
